  <prompt>REWRITTEN 2026-10-29. The first version (a 409 for `RestrictedContentOwnerTeamUnresolved`) rested on a wrong premise and is withdrawn: uac-r2 corrected themselves and the main session verified the code. `CheckVersionOwnerAsync` builds `new RecordOwnershipContext { Parents = ..., WhenUnfiled = KeepCreator }` and never sets `ChildEntityLogicalName`. 194b's restricted-content step (`RecordOwnershipResolver` ~:4050) returns the default-team answer unless `IsRestrictedContentTable(context.ChildEntityLogicalName)`, which is false for null. So a root-homed author's publish proceeds, no ownerid is bound, and the version stays the author's. That is the owner's D-197 ("Admin-tab authoring: the author wins ... including the root business unit"). Nothing pins it: if someone later passes `sprk_policyversion` as the child table (ForChild, ForRow), every root-homed author's publish starts failing with 503. Add that pin.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF engineer (Ontology Admin authoring tests).</role>
  <goal>A test fails if the `RecordOwnershipContext` that `CheckVersionOwnerAsync` passes to `IRecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveOwnerAsync` carries a non-null `ChildEntityLogicalName`. A one-line comment at the call cites D-197 and UAC round 137. No behaviour change.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      <ul>
        <li>Where: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ontology/OntologyAdminAuthoringService.cs`, `CheckVersionOwnerAsync` (~:1270-1290): the `ResolveOwnerAsync` call.</li>
        <li>The tests that already fake the resolver for this method: `tests/integration/auth/Ontology/OntologyAdminAuthoringSecureHoldTests.cs`. Capture the context there (or in a sibling file, in the same style) and assert on it.</li>
        <li>The resolver rule being protected: `RecordOwnershipResolver.cs` ~:4050 (`OrdinaryExitAsync`) and `IsRestrictedContentTable` ~:1781 (read only).</li>
      </ul>
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ontology/OntologyAdminAuthoringService.cs (comment only)</file>
      <file>tests/integration/auth/Ontology/OntologyAdminAuthoringSecureHoldTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-197">No behaviour change. The ownership question, the answers and the reason codes all stay as they are; only the comment and the test are added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md">Use `python`, never `python3`. No --no-verify, no git stash, no sub-agents. No Dataverse writes, no deploys. Never run the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add the test, asserting `ChildEntityLogicalName` is null and `WhenUnfiled` is `KeepCreator` on the captured context. Mutation-check: set `ChildEntityLogicalName = "sprk_policyversion"` at the call, confirm the test fails, then revert.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the comment. Run the filtered Ontology authoring tests. Open a PR into `docs/ontology-platform-design` citing D-197.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The pin test passes today and fails under the mutation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No production behaviour changes: the diff to OntologyAdminAuthoringService.cs is the comment only.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

